                        "entry_id": "64e423c6-e688-3998-a0ce-74c823c65280",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tropical flowering tree, cottonwood hibiscus (Talipariti tiliaceum, syn. Hibiscus tiliaceus), found in the South Pacific."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fa34745-626c-4a67-868c-5368e3f36e1c",
                                "sense_id": "7d10f7ce-3d5a-3ef5-b931-8e8276f0cf98",
                                "text": "Overhead was a thatch of buraos, and over these again palms brandished their bright fans, as I have seen a conjurer make himself a halo out of naked swords."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0beabe4-47ef-4528-8385-4a5893c06ca0",
                                "sense_id": "7d10f7ce-3d5a-3ef5-b931-8e8276f0cf98",
                                "text": "Tiares, hibiscuses, frangipani and flowered buraos smile to those who return and are not the least bit surprised by their faithfulness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6d446bd-c507-4ecd-8e65-224e2aaa3c21",
                                "sense_id": "7d10f7ce-3d5a-3ef5-b931-8e8276f0cf98",
                                "text": "There was a particular tree, the burao, used for fencing and the construction of indigenous huts, which had the ability to recover whatever the treatment it received."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
